  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the strongest baseline at 0.485 acc, while scgpt (config_007) underperforms at 0.411, confirming PCA as the preferred RNA encoder. Image-only (config_010) is very weak at 0.208, so multimodal gains will depend heavily on the RNA branch. Uncertainty: we have no evidence on whether multiprofile + aggregation improves over singleprofile for the best RNA encoder, and this axis underpins all subsequent multimodal and scvi/scgpt experiments. This experiment (config_002) tests multiprofile with the simplest aggregation (avgpool) while keeping the RNA encoder (pca_n2000) identical to config_001, cleanly isolating the profile-setting/aggregation effect without confounding. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it directly extends the strongest result, uses the least complex aggregation to avoid overfitting, and its outcome will guide whether to invest further in multiprofile + transformer or pivot to multimodal fusion with singleprofile."
}

